# Build output from the two test harnesses. Neither is shipped: what the
# NativePHP builder copies into a host app is `resources/`, and everything else
# here exists only so the decisions in those sources can be run.
#
# Unanchored on purpose. SwiftPM puts `.build` beside whichever directory it was
# invoked from, and Gradle does the same with `build` and `.gradle`, so a rule
# anchored at this directory misses the copy somebody's editor makes one level
# down — and a stray `.build` is 200MB of object files in a diff.
.build/
build/
.gradle/
.swiftpm/

# Composer's own output for this package. The plugin is consumed as a path
# repository from the repository root, so its dependencies are installed once at
# the root — a `vendor/` here is a stray from running composer inside this
# directory, and it is 20MB of somebody else's code in a diff.
/vendor/
/composer.lock
